# Normalize line endings on checkout so every platform sees identical bytes.
#
# Without this, a Windows runner checks text files out with CRLF and
# `gofmt -l .` reports all 368 Go files as unformatted, which is a false
# failure that says nothing about formatting. It also makes any other
# byte-comparing check (diff, grep, checksum) behave differently per platform.
#
# eol=lf controls what lands in the working tree; text=auto lets git detect
# binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The verification skill is tracked. It is not part of the release archive.
.cursor export-ignore
